                <pb facs="0604" n="509" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg509"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13412: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Peck</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-03-20T12:00:00+08:00">March 20,
                        1936—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received March 20—7 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>58. Shanghai’s 164 [<hi rendition="#italic">165</hi>], March 19, 4 p.m. Embassy
                    is informing Foreign Office and requesting that military authorities be directed
                    to afford adequate protection to Americans at Hungtung. Shanghai informed of
                    action taken.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
